$ drac.py -h
--- exit 0
--- stdout
usage: drac.py [-h] [-r | -ab] [-q] [-v] [-k PATTERN] [-cov]
               [-cov-include GLOB] [-cov-out DIR]
               files [files ...]

Record and compare dry-run output.

positional arguments:
  files              .toml case files or directories of them

options:
  -h, --help         show this help message and exit
  -r                 record (overwrite) snapshots
  -ab                compare the baseline script with the script under test
  -q                 one character per case; details only for failures
  -v                 also show the command line of each case
  -k PATTERN         only cases whose file::name matches (fnmatch, substring)
  -cov               also report which lines of the scripts under test ran
  -cov-include GLOB  Files to report (path or file-name glob, repeatable;
                     implies -cov); default: files under the directories of
                     the scripts under test
  -cov-out DIR       also write annotated listings to DIR (implies -cov)
--- stderr
